  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Duke Long tells Qi Sea Ancestor that if he joins Heavenly Court and makes outstanding contributions, he can obtain Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable’s true inheritance in the future.",
      "chapters": [
        1837
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_duke_long",
        "char_qi_sea_ancestor",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_primordial_origin_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Duke Long judges that wanting Primordial Origin’s true inheritance is a logical bargaining chip for a qi path cultivator. He tells Qi Sea Ancestor that the bulk of the true inheritance lies in creating Heavenly Court grotto-heaven, and that the rest is quite little and, after changing eras, no longer usable in the present world.",
      "chapters": [
        1839
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "negotiation-bait",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Duke Long compensates Qi Sea Ancestor with a large amount of qi path cultivation resources and gives one Primordial Origin true inheritance; that true inheritance is to be handed over in portions. Qi Sea Ancestor is Fang Yuan’s disguise in that truce.",
      "chapters": [
        1846
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "first-half-handover",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During the Eastern Sea contest over Dragon Palace, Fang Yuan obtains a Primordial Origin true inheritance segment after deceiving Duke Long; that segment contains only the first half, yet he praises it with deep admiration. From that half he understands Remote Antiquity Era qi path style as grand and powerful, and he judges Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable’s talent extraordinary. That part mainly talks about the killer move qi wall, Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable’s signature method; Duke Long hands it over under Fang Yuan’s firm attitude.",
      "chapters": [
        1855
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "qi-wall-segment",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "house_dragon_palace",
        "evt_era_remote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After the fate war, Fang Yuan obtains the remaining half of Primordial Origin’s true inheritance through Qin Ding Ling on an information path mortal Gu. In that remaining half, triple qi retraction is recorded. Qin Ding Ling treats the true inheritance as bait, knowing Qi Sea Ancestor will still need suitable qi path Immortal Gu from Heavenly Court treasuries to activate the recorded killer moves.",
      "chapters": [
        2005
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "remaining-half",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qin_ding_ling",
        "sys_information_path_mortal_gu",
        "move_triple_qi_retraction",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qi Sea Ancestor asks Heavenly Court for three rank eight Immortal Gu at once, the cores of Primordial Origin’s true inheritance; they are too valuable for ordinary payment. Qin Ding Ling gives heaven qi and earth qi Immortal Gu but refuses human qi Immortal Gu, keeping at least one as later bait, while noting that with two of the three he only needs human qi to use triple qi retraction.",
      "chapters": [
        2037
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "core-immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_earth_qi_immortal_gu",
        "gu_human_qi_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qi breath mountain was once used by Duke Long as part of Primordial Origin’s true inheritance and sent Purple Mountain True Monarch flying; Qi Sea Ancestor later uses that move as well.",
      "chapters": [
        2051
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "killer-move-battle-use",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_qi_breath_mountain",
        "char_purple_mountain_true_monarch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Although Qi Sea Ancestor obtained Primordial Origin’s true inheritance, Heavenly Court is too familiar with the killer moves in it, so those moves need to be modified.",
      "chapters": [
        2073
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "familiarity-limit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
